Wrote the design draft to `docs/designs/clo-323-sse-tail-f.md`. Seven sections per the persona contract: Problem, Goals/Non-goals, Architecture (with ASCII data-flow diagram and concrete Rust types), Public API surface (route registration, handler signature, internal helpers, frontend script, the single new dep `notify`), Test plan (named unit + integration tests, manual steps, pre-merge gate), Migration (additive, no flag), and five genuinely open questions covering keepalive helper choice, chunk ceiling, fan-out, macOS FSEvents latency risk, and per-run connection caps.
